#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Culture - Arts" tvg-id="1861337863" tvg-name="Exiled in Guernsey from October 1855‚ Hugo completes 'Les Misérables' with the help of his lifelong mistress‚ Juliette Drouet. In Paris‚ art is under attack: Gustave Flaubert's 'Madame Bovary'‚ Baudelaire's 'Les fleurs du mal' and Manet's 'Le déjeuner sur l'herbe' are all censored.<br/>From 21.12.2024 22:39" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Romantics of Paris (4/4) - Emancipation (1855-1874) (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (21.12.2024)
