#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Planet Earth" tvg-id="291033816" tvg-name="The Wadden Sea National Park‚ which stretches from the Netherlands to Denmark‚ is punctuated by a string of islands endowed with a unique geological feature: due to their very low elevation‚ they are are regularly flooded at high tide. This unique characteristic results in a rare biosphere‚where mudflats‚ sandbanks‚ meadows and salt marshes succeed one another.<br/>From 30.09.2021 12:04" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",The Halligen Islands Under Water (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (30.09.2021)
